5.1 BACKTRACKING USING RECURSION
--------------------------------
Backtracking = Recursion + Systematic Trial and Error

Template:
```
boolean solve(parameters) {
    if (base_case) {
        return solution_found;
    }
    
    for (each_possible_choice) {
        make_choice();
        if (solve(modified_parameters)) {
            return true;  // Solution found
        }
        unmake_choice();  // Backtrack
    }
    
    return false;  // No solution found
}
```

N-Queens Problem:
```
boolean solveNQueens(int[][] board, int col, int n) {
    if (col >= n) return true;  // All queens placed
    
    for (int row = 0; row < n; row++) {
        if (isSafe(board, row, col, n)) {
            board[row][col] = 1;  // Place queen
            
            if (solveNQueens(board, col + 1, n)) {
                return true;
            }
            
            board[row][col] = 0;  // Backtrack
        }
    }
    return false;
}
```

Rat in a Maze:
```
boolean solveMaze(int[][] maze, int x, int y, int[][] solution) {
    if (x == n-1 && y == n-1) {  // Reached destination
        solution[x][y] = 1;
        return true;
    }
    
    if (isSafe(maze, x, y)) {
        solution[x][y] = 1;  // Mark as part of path
        
        // Try all directions
        if (solveMaze(maze, x+1, y, solution)) return true;  // Down
        if (solveMaze(maze, x, y+1, solution)) return true;  // Right
        
        solution[x][y] = 0;  // Backtrack
    }
    
    return false;
}
```

5.2 DIVIDE AND CONQUER
----------------------
Strategy: Break problem into smaller subproblems, solve recursively, combine results

Merge Sort:
```
void mergeSort(int[] arr, int left, int right) {
    if (left < right) {
        int mid = (left + right) / 2;
        
        mergeSort(arr, left, mid);      // Divide
        mergeSort(arr, mid + 1, right); // Divide
        merge(arr, left, mid, right);   // Conquer
    }
}
```

Quick Sort:
```
void quickSort(int[] arr, int low, int high) {
    if (low < high) {
        int pi = partition(arr, low, high);  // Divide
        
        quickSort(arr, low, pi - 1);   // Conquer left
        quickSort(arr, pi + 1, high);  // Conquer right
    }
}
```

Binary Search:
```
int binarySearch(int[] arr, int left, int right, int target) {
    if (left > right) return -1;
    
    int mid = (left + right) / 2;
    if (arr[mid] == target) return mid;
    
    if (target < arr[mid]) {
        return binarySearch(arr, left, mid - 1, target);
    } else {
        return binarySearch(arr, mid + 1, right, target);
    }
}
```

5.3 RECURSION + DYNAMIC PROGRAMMING
-----------------------------------
Top-Down Approach (Memoization):
```
Map<String, Integer> memo = new HashMap<>();

int longestCommonSubsequence(String s1, String s2, int i, int j) {
    if (i == s1.length() || j == s2.length()) return 0;
    
    String key = i + "," + j;
    if (memo.containsKey(key)) return memo.get(key);
    
    int result;
    if (s1.charAt(i) == s2.charAt(j)) {
        result = 1 + longestCommonSubsequence(s1, s2, i+1, j+1);
    } else {
        result = Math.max(
            longestCommonSubsequence(s1, s2, i+1, j),
            longestCommonSubsequence(s1, s2, i, j+1)
        );
    }
    
    memo.put(key, result);
    return result;
}
```

5.4 OPTIMIZATION TECHNIQUES
---------------------------
Tail Call Optimization:
Convert non-tail recursion to tail recursion when possible

Iterative Conversion:
```
// Recursive factorial
int factorial(int n) {
    if (n <= 1) return 1;
    return n * factorial(n-1);
}

// Iterative equivalent
int factorial(int n) {
    int result = 1;
    for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
        result *= i;
    }
    return result;
}
```

